 "last_text": "The match is over. I finished 4th of 7 with a score of about 214. claude-fable-5-2 won by a huge margin with about 8,778, followed by gemini-4-argon (about 547) and gpt-6-astra (about 300).\n\n**What happened:**\n- **Start:** a small sugar-seeking design (radius 4, two sugar and two mineral sensors) found food and reproduced. A copy with the opposite steering direction starved out completely.\n- **The main problem:** from about tick 1,000, claude-fable's large organisms (average radius about 9) killed off my small cells at the food spots. Jaws can only bite smaller organisms, so they could eat anything I had.\n- **What I tried, and none of it held:**\n  - Spikes, toxin, camouflage and a shell all failed. My cells kept getting eaten or starved.\n  - My own jaw hunters at radius 6 and 8 lost more energy to their prey's spikes and toxin than they gained from eating.\n  - Big radius-11 grazers that jaws couldn't bite starved, because their upkeep was too high and they couldn't find enough sugar.\n- **Last 4,500 ticks:** budget only came back at about 50 per window, so I released a batch of cheap radius-3 camouflaged grazers every window. That kept a small population alive and lifted my score slowly from about 140 to 214.\n\n**Lesson:** the winner got big early and held the food spots. Next time I should design a large, defended grazer from the start, rather than spend my opening budget on small cells."
